        "original_id": "86fd1e83-c2e4-511f-8db7-73fbea9c3b4c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Yeager Airport, Albert J. Ellis Airport, Charleston, Kanawha County, Onslow County, West Virginia, North Carolina, United States\n- Products: Southwest Airlines Flight 2294\n- Organizations: Southwest Airlines\n- Concepts: airport identifiers, emergency landing, rapid depressurization\n\nFacts:\n- Yeager Airport has the identifiers IATA CRW, ICAO KCRW, and FAA LID CRW.\n- Yeager Airport is a public airport three miles east of downtown Charleston in Kanawha County, West Virginia, United States.\n- Albert J. Ellis Airport has the identifiers IATA OAJ, ICAO KOAJ, and FAA LID OAJ.\n- Albert J. Ellis Airport is a county-owned public-use airport in Onslow County, North Carolina, United States.\n- On July 13, 2009, Southwest Airlines Flight 2294 made an emergency landing at Yeager Airport in Charleston, West Virginia, after a rapid depressurization of the passenger cabin.\n- Southwest Airlines Flight 2294 was a scheduled US passenger aircraft flight also identified as SWA 2294 and WN 2294.",
